menu "Hunter RMT"
    config HUNTER_RMT_GPIO
        int "GPIO pin connected to REM"
        default 4
        help
            The GPIO that drives the Hunter controller's REM terminal.
            Default is GPIO 4 — any free output-capable GPIO works.

    config HUNTER_RMT_INVERT
        bool "Invert RMT signal (for opto-isolator)"
        default n
        help
            Inverts the logic level of every RMT symbol. Enable this if
            you're driving the REM pin through an opto-isolator (PC817,
            TLP281, etc.) which inverts the signal: ESP32 HIGH → LED on
            → transistor conducts → REM pulled LOW.
endmenu
